  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). MISPREMISED TODAY. The code is as described -- _merge_with_user_override keys on (module, name, kind) without the label (taint.py:2253-2262); disclosure filter verify_claims.py:5996-6001 -- but the stated repro cannot happen: every two-label source today is one of 12 JS/TS ATTRIBUTE rows (document.location, window.location...), and the user source loader _load_source_yaml (taint.py:1766-1815) builds only functions:/methods: entries (by design: WI-jojis wont_do chose auto-derivation). Live check: a user file with attributes: [location] (or functions: [location]) left both claims violated, identical to baseline. It becomes live when a function/method row gains two labels -- WI-zidam's argv change does exactly that (rust env::args, haskell getArgs, elixir System.argv, erlang init:get_argument*, argparse parse_args); even then the drop is disclosed (displaced_shipped_entry), not a silent false confirm. Hence isbefore WI-zidam. Split out: the requires_target_kind / requires_mode name collision -> WI-dinop; the silently-ignored attributes: key in user source files -> WI-rinaz. P3 -> P4."  # 65dd
